{"kind":"overview","sections":[{"action":{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/tutorials\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/Chapter0-Setup","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"Get started","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"Get started","type":"text"}]},"title":"Build an Immersive Space Above the Clouds","backgroundImage":"overthecloud_thumbnail.png","image":"overthecloud_thumbnail.png","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"code":"RealityView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"ImmersiveSpace","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in visionOS to build an immersive environment that feels like floating among clouds.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Follow the project from start to finish: model shared state, add and preload assets, arrange and animate 3D content, and connect the window controls to immersive transitions.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"–","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Before you begin, download the assets in ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Chapter 1"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" and add them to your Xcode project.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can test the app in Simulator without Apple Vision Pro. To fully experience the depth and immersion of the space, run the app on a device.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"hero"},{"name":null,"chapters":[{"image":"ch1_preview.png","tutorials":["doc:\/\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/tutorials\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/Chapter0-Setup"],"name":"1. Set up the project and assets","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a visionOS app and connect the supplied sky texture and Reality Composer Pro cloud package to the app target. Complete this setup before writing the code in the remaining chapters."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"image":"overthecloud_icon_front.png","tutorials":["doc:\/\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/tutorials\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/Chapter1-AppModel"],"name":"2. Model the app state","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro to design an "},{"code":"AppModel","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that manages immersive space state across the app."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"image":"ch3_preview.png","tutorials":["doc:\/\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/tutorials\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/Chapter2-SkyAssetCache"],"name":"3. Preload and cache assets","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Implement a "},{"code":"SkyAssetCache","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that asynchronously preloads and caches the sky texture and cloud entities."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"image":"ch4_preview.png","tutorials":["doc:\/\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/tutorials\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/Chapter3-ImmersiveView"],"name":"4. Build the immersive content","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"code":"RealityView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to distribute a sky sphere and clouds, then add a floating animation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"image":"skyview_img.png","tutorials":["doc:\/\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/tutorials\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/Chapter4-ContentView"],"name":"5. Build the main window and transitions","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Adapt the UI to asset loading state and implement a button that opens and closes the immersive space."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"image":"contentview_img.png","tutorials":["doc:\/\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/tutorials\/2026TechMap_tutorial\/Chapter5-OvertheCloudApp"],"name":"6. Configure the app entry point","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register a "},{"code":"WindowGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and an "},{"code":"ImmersiveSpace","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to connect all the app’s components."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"image